PART 10: SAFE STUDENT HANDOVER
==================================================

Implement a realistic student handover system.

A student must NOT require a smartphone.

The student must NOT need to scan a QR code or enter a PIN.

Create three configurable dismissal policies:

1. GUARDIAN REQUIRED

- Driver marks arrival at drop-off.
- Parent is notified through a simulated notification.
- Authorized guardian provides a one-time PIN.
- Driver enters PIN.
- System verifies the PIN.
- Handover is recorded.

2. AUTHORIZED ADULT REQUIRED

- Parent registers approved pickup persons.
- Administrator approves the authorized persons.
- Driver verifies the pickup person according to school policy.
- Record the handover.

3. INDEPENDENT DISMISSAL

- Parent and school authorize independent dismissal.
- Driver records the student's dismissal.
- No guardian PIN is required.
- Record the driver, time and status.

PIN requirements:
- Unique one-time PIN.
- Expiry.
- Attempt limits.
- Verification history.
- No permanent PIN display.
- No PIN for independent dismissal.
- No successful handover on incorrect PIN.

For this demo, notification delivery can be simulated.

